# Memory

- At the start of a session, read the `memory://` resource from the
  `memory-inject` MCP server that matches your working directory
  (plus `memory://global`) — or call `memory_search` — before starting work.
- Use `memory_search` to inspect topic files or search existing lessons
  before recording new ones so you don't duplicate entries.
- Record durable, verified learnings (pitfalls, decisions, project
  specifics) with `memory_note`, passing `directory` = the absolute path
  of the repo you are working in. One tight bullet per note; global,
  cross-project rules use `global: true`. To park an unreviewed candidate
  mid-session for later curation, pass `stage: true`.
